<BaseLayout title="AI Systems Observatory | Governance Commons" description="Evidence-first model, agent and protocol catalog and benchmark methodology roadmap.">
<style>.observatory-tile {cursor:pointer;position:relative}.observatory-tile h2 a::after {content:"";position:absolute;inset:0}.observatory-tile:focus-within {outline:2px solid currentColor;outline-offset:3px}.observatory-tile .text-link {position:relative;z-index:1}</style>
<section class="section white" style="padding-top:150px">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">AI Systems Observatory · In development</p><h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.6rem,6vw,5rem)">Compare models, agents and protocols—with evidence.</h1><p>We are preparing versioned catalogs and reproducible comparisons. No benchmark rankings have been released here yet.</p></div>
  <div class="intro-grid">
    <article class="surface observatory-tile"><h2><a href="/observatory/models">Models →</a></h2><p>Exact versions, capabilities, source dates and independently reported benchmark context. A model score does not establish agent performance.</p><a class="text-link" href="/observatory/models">Browse model sources →</a></article>
    <article class="surface observatory-tile"><h2><a href="/observatory/agents">Agents →</a></h2><p>Agent implementations, dependencies, task performance and observed reliability. Roster ingestion will follow schema and provenance verification.</p><a class="text-link" href="/observatory/agents">Browse agent sources →</a></article>
    <article class="surface observatory-tile"><h2><a href="/observatory/protocols">Protocols →</a></h2><p>Versioned interoperability and governance evidence comparisons, including GC proposals evaluated under the same criteria as external protocols.</p><a class="text-link" href="/observatory/protocols">Browse protocol sources →</a></article>
  </div>
  <div class="section-heading" style="margin-top:45px"><h2>Benchmark methodology</h2><p>Rankings will only compare matching evaluation tasks and conditions. Each result must disclose its evaluator, test version, sample size, model snapshot, runtime, success criteria, latency, cost, provenance and limitations. Missing measurements mean “not evaluated,” not zero. Vendor-reported and independently reproduced results will be visibly distinguished.</p><p>Capability, security, interoperability and governance evidence are separate dimensions—not one universal score.</p></div>
  <div class="section-heading" style="margin-top:45px"><h2>Source and freshness status</h2><p>GC's existing Agent Roster is a curated, versioned source with 32 paid/free model selections across four software-development roles. Its source declares a last manual verification date of <strong>August 7, 2026</strong>. The monthly scheduled workflow opens a review issue; it does not automatically update rankings or execute performance tests. The Agent Matrix is a separate governance specification, not a benchmark leaderboard.</p><p><strong>Public ranking status:</strong> No roster recommendations are republished here until the underlying model IDs, provider claims, evaluation evidence, publication rights and current availability have been independently reviewed.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/governancecommons/governance-commons-registry">Inspect the public GC registry →</a></p></div>
  <div class="surface notice"><strong>Publication status:</strong> Catalog v0.4.0 offers 14 editorial source-index records across models, agents and protocols. Automated feeds, Agent Matrix / Agent Roster integration, benchmark runs, and automated updates are not yet active. No rankings or claims of external certification are offered.</div>
  <div class="actions" style="margin-top:28px"><a class="button ink" href="/ecosystem">Explore the ecosystem directory</a></div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>